      "side": 1,
      "message": "In a case where:\n - Service was received at t\u003d0s with ttl\u003d120\n - Service was re-queried at t\u003d110s\n\nThen I think the service should still expire at t\u003d120s. The bug we\u0027re trying to fix is a case where, even if we query every 20s, if the CPU is sleeping during t\u003d[100s, 121s] we shouldn\u0027t mark the service expired immediately on wakeup. But in the case where there\u0027s no sleep, expiry doesn\u0027t need to be delayed.\n\nSo I think the condition should be \"was the service queried after its last receipt time (from SRV record), and was that query more than 2 seconds ago\".\n\nIn which case `mLastQueryTime` should be changed to `mFirstQueryTimeAfterLastUpdate`",
